WEBVTT

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.750
Karte 2 - A Funeral, The Procession Game

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.200
The phone! The phone's ringing!

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.470
Let it ring.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.110
Why do you always have to do that?

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.380
I'm not in at the moment. If you are
in need of medical attention...

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.420
please leave a number where
you can be reached, your name...

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.720
the seriousness of your condition and
how much you are able to afford.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.710
I will return your call
as soon as possible.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.760
The more I doubt,
the more I believe you.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:43.840
But before that...

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.970
The more I lose,
the more I yearn.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.580
Let me say goodbye.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:02:01.250
All I want is to keep
on watching you smile...

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:11.460
As I hold you in these
arms called memories.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.800
We leave on a journey now,
through the times of dark...

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.640
To the other side of the darkness...

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.840
Not yet today,
but tomorrow is so far.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:30.150
Darkest time, just before the sunrise.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:39.530
If they ask you your name,
answer, "I am a traveler."

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:48.660
That's all I want you to say.
That's all...

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:57.010
Don't tell them where you're going.
Don't leave any parting words.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:07.020
They will remember you
as the one who vanished.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.390
I'm not lonely because I know...

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:15.930
In the end, you're always alone.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:20.500
That's why I close my heart
and end up there.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.940
Darkest time, just before the sunrise.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.680
We leave on a journey now,
through the times of dark...

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.120
To the other side of the darkness...

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.590
I'm not lonely because I know...

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:47.130
In the end, you're always alone.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:51.530
We leave on a journey now,
through the times of dark...

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.830
To the other side of the darkness...

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:26.930
It was sheer coincidence I
happened to drive through S-city...

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.160
a place famous for its snow festival.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.310
I was returning from
examining a patient...

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.140
in a small rural town far
outside the city.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:40.310
I misread the signpost in the snowfall
and it led me to this city.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.760
Can you tell me how to
get to the airport from here?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.270
Sure, but there aren't any flights
leaving at this time of night!

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.370
Hey, I doubt he's lost.
I bet he's just trying to pick us up!

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:14.840
Come on.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.410
Ew! What a perv!

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.220
Take Park Avenue, then turn
right onto the interstate...

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.190
Good luck!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.150
Rie, are you all right?

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.760
Rie Fujinami.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.030
She was a sophomore at
a private all-girl high school.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.660
Laceration of the forehead region.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.640
Four millimeters deep,
five centimeters wide.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.900
I immediately administered
emergency medical aid.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:18.140
Since it was in a visible area, I used
an intradermal continuous suture.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.890
Calmly listen to what I say.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:36.360
After the bandages come off, your
forehead will have a scar for a while.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:41.170
It might be noticeable at first but
it'll only be for a short while.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.260
It'll be gone without a trace in a year.
I assure you.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.200
Okay? There's nothing to worry about.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:52.670
You're so sweet.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:08.560
Later on, it took another coincidence
for me to remember those girls again.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.830
Six months passed and
the hot summer was already here.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.480
Hey.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:29.880
Is this seat available?

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.780
I never thought I'd bump
into a friend at a place like this!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.760
Stop looking so annoyed! It's been so
long since we've last seen each other.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.490
So tell me, how's the unlicensed
medical practice going?

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:51.400
Just my luck. He's Lt. Takasugi of the
Metropolitan Police Department.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.270
You're in a non-smoking section.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:57.270
Don't be such a hard-ass. I bend the
rules for you all the time, don't I?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.080
Do you have a patient in S-city?

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.140
No, I'm switching planes at S-city.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.590
I'm going to be at the S-city
police department for a while.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.120
Swing by before you leave.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.730
Let's have a drink for old time's sake.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:15.390
I'm in Investigations, Section Four.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.500
Section Four?

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.360
It's similar to tracking
down people in your field.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.560
Except I track down
drugs that are destroying lives.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:55.190
I stopped in at the S-city Police
Department, but Lt. Takasugi was out.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.470
Since he's not someone
worth waiting for...

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.970
I decided to continue on to the airport.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:07.910
This was the second time
I had come through S-city.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.620
It was a city that
I would only pass through.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.550
Other than that, it had no other
significant meaning to me.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.290
Airport, please.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.420
Wait!

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.330
Wait! Taxi!

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.760
Do you know that girl, Sir?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.030
Hey wait! Taxi!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:38.470
Please!

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.610
I've been waiting for you!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:53.620
See? The scar really
isn't noticeable anymore!

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.520
It'll be gone entirely
in another six months.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:01.130
I showed it to a doctor in the city and
he said it was stitched beautifully!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.030
He even said it was perfect and that
there aren't that many doctors...

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:08.270
in the world who can do it as well as
you did! He told me I was really lucky!

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.010
I had no idea you were
such an amazing doctor!

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.590
I didn't recognize you at first.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:29.860
Yeah, I changed my hairstyle.
If I do this... See?

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:32.330
It hides it really well.

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:35.570
Perms aren't allowed
at our school, but...

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:38.600
I was able to get permission,
thanks to this scar.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:42.800
I should be thanking you for that too!

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:54.550
How are your friends?
Are they doing well?

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.460
You said you've been waiting for me...

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:09.060
I've been waiting for you
for two months at that park.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.930
Day and night... All day long...

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.270
I hoped you'd come back...
Someday, I knew you'd come back...

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:24.250
For two months? That's crazy.
I only came by this city by chance.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.650
Then you showed up!
I knew you would!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.880
I'm so glad I waited!

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.020
Please, I need your help!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.480
Did you hear about the accident
at Mt. Sennin two months ago?

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.780
I haven't...

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.910
It made headlines in
the local paper here but...

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.120
The suspension bridge snapped, and...

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:06.220
Yumiko fell eighty meters, all the way
to the bottom of the ravine.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:08.830
I was saved because
I was walking behind her.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:18.400
Two months... For two months,
Yumiko has been in a coma.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.300
The doctors at that hospital
say it's hopeless.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.100
No matter what I ask them, they keep
saying it's hopeless, it's hopeless...

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:29.110
I want you to save Yumiko.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.680
She shouldn't have to live life as a
vegetable... It's not fair to her...

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:41.120
Plus I can't bear to see another friend
die...

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:43.320
Another?

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:47.730
Stop it!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:51.730
Yuki was killed instantly when a
speeding car hit her three months ago.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.900
You won't believe this, but...

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:58.030
Kaori stepped on to the train tracks
and committed suicide ten days later.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.600
Outside of S-city there's a residential
area with a population of 150,000.

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:30.570
The general hospital was located in
that area, on a large piece of land.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:37.150
Dr. Udagawa. Dr. Udagawa.
Please report to Radiology.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:42.450
You'd say it was a public hospital
by how big and well-equipped it was,

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.510
and yet this hospital
is privately owned.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.180
Nice lap, Tokio!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.420
Keep this up and you'll be able to
qualify for the Suzuka Race!

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:21.690
Suzuka Race, eh?

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.620
Okay, thirty minute break!

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.470
Straighten out the spoiler
for me, will ya?

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.200
I can't get enough pickup
on the straightaways.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:30.130
OK, Tokio!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.430
It's concentration that matters, Tokio!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.140
Hi, Tokio. You have a phone call.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.970
It's from your hospital.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.820
What? I don't know anything
about this guy!!

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.090
But he insisted you requested him.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.350
Doctor! Doctor!

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:27.690
What?

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:29.790
He went into ward D?

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:30.430
Yes.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.460
I gave strict instructions to never let
unauthorized personnel in that area!

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.170
Yes, I understand but...

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:39.070
Doctor! Doctor! Please wait!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.910
Who are you?

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:50.640
I'm her physician.
Yumiko Inoue to be specific.

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.350
I took my time reading over
her clinical charts...

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:58.210
Were you the one who wrote this?

00:15:58.660 --> 00:15:59.210
Yes I was!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:02.630
I hope you don't mind,
but while I was waiting for you...

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.320
I did a simple urinalysis and
ran a blood test on her.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:06.790
What?

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:09.730
I got some interesting results back...

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.360
that weren't included in
these clinical charts.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.340
Tokio Umetani.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.710
He's an average surgeon that graduated
from a third-rate medical school...

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.910
But he took after his late father
who built this hospital...

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:27.280
and became its second president. He's
just the type to cause some trouble.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:35.850
I've heard of you...

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.860
Yes, my father told me about you.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:40.660
An unlicensed physician...

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.500
and yet he's infamous in
the illegal medical world.

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:45.140
A man who lives like a parasite...

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.500
Black Jack...

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.140
Yes, you must be Black Jack!

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.510
Gonna extort me? Blackmail me?

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:57.840
Well I'm not having it! I'm not going
to let you get anything out of me!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:03.190
I want to perform an
operation on Yumiko Inoue.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.820
My surgical fee is fifty million yen.

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:08.350
I will expect the payment
to be paid by your hospital.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:10.460
You've got to be kidding me!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.200
I'm not kidding you.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.570
I'll call the cops.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:15.470
Go ahead.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:18.130
Then I'll have to publicize the results
from the urinalysis and blood test...

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.900
that were left out
in her clinical charts.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:30.210
It's useless. She's a vegetable.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.590
The nerve fibers in her brain
have been completely destroyed.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:36.920
An operation would be
absolutely useless!

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:42.020
I've resuscitated comatose
patients twice before.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.920
She's only sixteen years old.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:50.070
No one has the right to take away
her life by keeping her this way.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:05.280
Isn't it great, Yumiko? Dr. Black Jack
said he'll operate on you!

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:09.240
Thank you, Doctor!
Thank you so much!

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:10.610
I love you!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.350
I love you!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:17.020
For the first time ever,
I met a wonderful man!

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:37.380
The operation is scheduled for tomorrow
night.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.040
You should go home.
Your parents will be worried.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.180
But there's no one waiting
for me at the house!

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:51.400
My school is a boarding school.
My family lives in Tokyo.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:54.730
I've been living by myself
since I was in junior high.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.300
Same goes for Yumiko.

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:04.470
Well, in Yumiko's case...

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.910
her father's a businessman;
her parents live in Chicago.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.240
Our school caters to parents who
have money but don't have time...

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.450
for their kids. The entire country
knows our school's rap.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.220
A.K.A. "The Orphanage School"!

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:34.430
Let me stay over! Let me stay
in your hotel room tonight!

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:36.910
No.

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.250
Right here. Thank you.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:54.450
Hold on.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.860
This is a school dorm?
That's really hard to believe.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:06.170
Going to a boarding school is just
an excuse to get your parent...

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:10.610
to pay for a 'Study Room' in the city.
That's what you do nowadays.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.310
Everyone wants to keep their privacy.

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.100
Night!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.410
Oh that's right!

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:25.120
You know it's fine by me if
you want to stay over in my room!

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:28.690
Look...

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:34.320
Doctor...

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:39.330
I bet you're thinking I've
never had sex. Aren't you?

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.570
Bleah!

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.140
Good night!

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:23.540
I can't help it.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:27.240
Something came up and
I have to operate tomorrow.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:32.290
NO! You promised me you'd
come home on yesterday's flight!

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:36.120
What am I supposed to do with the
special curry I made for you?

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.560
I put so much love into making it! Well?

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.190
Depending on how it goes...

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:43.730
I might have to stay an
additional week after the surgery.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.200
Argh! Drop dead!

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:50.010
That would be nice, wouldn't it?

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:53.240
I'm dumping you! We're through!
I'll cheat on you!

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:55.140
JERK JERK JERK JERK JERK!

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:07.560
I heard you came by
the office yesterday.

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:10.950
There we go...

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:12.720
There's beer in the fridge
if you want it.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.630
No, I'm all set with alcohol right now.

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:20.130
Is it true you're operating
on Yumiko Inoue?

00:22:22.310 --> 00:22:25.900
I did a little legwork. I asked the
hospital staff when I heard the rumor.

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:28.850
I have no idea.
It has nothing to do with me.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:34.610
Relax! I'm not in charge of arresting
unlicensed physicians anymore.

00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:38.520
There's one thing I want to ask you.

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.330
Was this an operation
requested by the hospital?

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:47.000
No...

00:22:52.670 --> 00:22:55.230
Next time, let's make it
a point to go get a drink.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:22:57.400
Later.

00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:17.730
I'm cold...

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:19.260
Yumiko...

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:26.630
Yuki, no... Kaori, no.
Don't open the window...

00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:29.660
The wind is so cold...

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:41.490
I'm so cold...

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:54.430
It's so warm...

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:08.500
Come in.

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:12.210
Doctor, we have a favor
we'd like to ask you.

00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:15.040
What is it?

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:19.320
We heard that Yumiko Inoue's
operation is scheduled for tonight.

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:22.420
Will the man who was here
yesterday be performing the surgery?

00:24:24.030 --> 00:24:25.100
Yes.

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.770
Is he Black Jack?

00:24:27.770 --> 00:24:29.570
His features, his age, his clothes...

00:24:29.570 --> 00:24:32.160
they're all as I heard when
I was at the University Hospital.

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:34.870
So what about it?

00:24:34.870 --> 00:24:38.070
We'd like to witness the
proceedings of the operation!

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:41.250
No, please let us assist him!

00:24:41.250 --> 00:24:43.450
People call him a genius!

00:24:43.450 --> 00:24:45.640
I want to see it with my own eyes!

00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:47.850
He's an unlicensed physician!

00:24:47.850 --> 00:24:51.520
Doctor! Please! Please!
Doctor! Please Doctor! Doctor!

00:24:51.520 --> 00:24:55.760
I don't care! If you want permission,
go ask him yourselves!

00:25:29.490 --> 00:25:30.720
Dr. Black Jack.

00:25:31.460 --> 00:25:32.990
Doctor! Doctor! Doctor!

00:25:35.270 --> 00:25:38.290
At 6:47 P.M. the sun set.

00:25:38.840 --> 00:25:41.470
Five minutes later, we started
Yumiko Inoue's intracranial...

00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:43.340
hematoma elimination surgery.

00:26:01.130 --> 00:26:03.120
As per the other doctors' request...

00:26:03.330 --> 00:26:04.820
I allowed two anesthesiologists...

00:26:05.330 --> 00:26:06.960
three surgeons...

00:26:07.370 --> 00:26:10.130
and four nurses to be
present during the surgery.

00:26:10.600 --> 00:26:14.800
However, I alone will perform the
surgery in its entirety...

00:26:15.410 --> 00:26:18.710
because that is how I always work.

00:26:22.680 --> 00:26:23.340
Let's begin.

00:27:31.980 --> 00:27:33.450
I see...

00:27:34.050 --> 00:27:36.610
You must have spent a fortune
on the President's Office.

00:27:37.460 --> 00:27:38.620
Who are you?

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:42.730
I'm Dr. Black Jack's manager.

00:27:43.260 --> 00:27:45.030
There's always something to learn...

00:27:45.030 --> 00:27:48.430
by watching the doctor's
brilliant techniques.

00:27:48.770 --> 00:27:50.530
That's why you're watching it too right?

00:27:51.440 --> 00:27:54.810
You're always playing around and
you're a crappy second president...

00:27:54.810 --> 00:27:56.030
but you're still a physician, I guess.

00:27:56.410 --> 00:27:57.270
What did you say?

00:27:57.880 --> 00:28:01.180
Calm down. Don't get so angry.
Just because I'm being honest...

00:28:03.050 --> 00:28:05.040
Get out of here or I'll call security!

00:28:07.050 --> 00:28:08.080
Oh come on!

00:28:09.150 --> 00:28:10.920
Fine. Fine! I'll leave!

00:28:12.790 --> 00:28:14.550
Study hard!

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:20.320
Gradually add one unit of plasma.

00:28:21.470 --> 00:28:21.900
Yes.

00:28:22.730 --> 00:28:24.220
Add gamma globulin.

00:28:24.500 --> 00:28:24.760
Yes.

00:28:26.270 --> 00:28:27.000
Check ICP.

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:32.200
Pulse is 60. Blood Pressure
100 over 50. ICP is stable.

00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:35.740
All right. We will now perform a
surgical evacuation...

00:28:35.810 --> 00:28:38.280
of the hematoma that is applying
pressure to the brain neurons.

00:28:41.420 --> 00:28:45.560
It's imperative to prevent oscillation
and stimulation to the patient.

00:28:45.560 --> 00:28:50.090
The slightest injury to the nerve and
she will be a comatose patient forever.

00:28:50.630 --> 00:28:51.250
Yes!

00:28:52.830 --> 00:28:55.730
Lights, centered at two thousand lux.

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:58.730
Centered at two thousand lux!

00:29:19.060 --> 00:29:19.990
Please, God.

00:29:41.250 --> 00:29:44.580
Please take care of her.
That's what they said...

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:49.320
Last night, when I called
the patient's parents in Chicago...

00:29:49.390 --> 00:29:51.950
to get their consent for the operation,
that's what they said to me.

00:29:56.090 --> 00:29:58.820
"Please take care of her," they said...

00:30:02.400 --> 00:30:03.800
Please take care of her...

00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:06.470
When their daughter might die...

00:30:08.170 --> 00:30:09.570
Take care of her...

00:30:16.050 --> 00:30:19.350
Although they are a family,
human life is an individual thing.

00:30:21.190 --> 00:30:26.920
Humans instinctively know they cannot
prevent the inevitability of death.

00:30:29.460 --> 00:30:33.930
I even know myself that all man
can do is mourn death...

00:30:33.930 --> 00:30:36.590
and take a moment to shed a tear.

00:30:37.100 --> 00:30:38.360
Perhaps...

00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:43.000
Perhaps that's why I'm
doing something like this.

00:30:45.280 --> 00:30:50.080
To leave proof that efforts were made
to keep the dying ones alive...

00:30:50.150 --> 00:30:54.080
before displaying our grief
over the passing of life...

00:30:55.050 --> 00:30:56.210
Futile as it may be...

00:30:56.290 --> 00:31:01.220
there are people in this world who find
a glimmer of hope in these attempts...

00:31:26.080 --> 00:31:28.350
It's almost dawn...

00:31:31.160 --> 00:31:34.180
This is one hell of an operation.
It's been ten hours already...

00:31:38.630 --> 00:31:41.260
Have one of these. It's still warm.

00:31:42.330 --> 00:31:42.960
No thank you.

00:31:45.370 --> 00:31:47.100
I have ogura bread if you want one.

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:50.730
Red bean donuts?

00:32:06.020 --> 00:32:06.890
We finished.

00:32:13.900 --> 00:32:15.930
Move the patient to
the intensive care unit.

00:32:15.930 --> 00:32:19.400
Antibiotics to prevent
postoperative infection and
also an intracranial pressure check.

00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:20.000
Yes!

00:32:22.440 --> 00:32:24.840
I'm going to lie down
and get some sleep here.

00:32:28.580 --> 00:32:29.100
Let's hurry!

00:32:33.650 --> 00:32:34.550
Yumiko!

00:32:36.850 --> 00:32:37.650
Yumiko!

00:32:40.530 --> 00:32:41.650
Hey, you guys!

00:32:41.730 --> 00:32:43.850
Move! Please get out of the way!

00:32:47.530 --> 00:32:48.500
Yumiko!

00:33:18.400 --> 00:33:19.090
All right, let's go!

00:33:19.700 --> 00:33:20.130
Roger.

00:33:25.300 --> 00:33:27.600
He's probably going to
the race circuit as usual.

00:33:28.040 --> 00:33:29.800
We're already on to him.

00:33:30.070 --> 00:33:32.040
The rest is all timing.

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:43.950
Doctor, you won't believe it!

00:33:45.690 --> 00:33:50.560
Yumiko ate two apples! She said they're
delicious! That they taste great!!

00:33:53.530 --> 00:33:55.800
The operation was a success.

00:33:58.270 --> 00:33:59.430
Three days after the surgery...

00:33:59.500 --> 00:34:02.230
Yumiko was moved to a
private room from the ICU.

00:34:02.910 --> 00:34:04.240
Her condition was steadily improving.

00:34:04.240 --> 00:34:06.940
Fortunately she did not develop
a postoperative infection...

00:34:07.010 --> 00:34:08.740
nor did her
intracranial pressure rise.

00:34:09.410 --> 00:34:11.610
She was always smiling happily.

00:34:14.190 --> 00:34:18.490
What slightly concerns me is that she
shows signs of dementia...

00:34:19.720 --> 00:34:22.280
and because of that, she says
strange things occasionally.

00:34:24.360 --> 00:34:27.730
The party... We should
decorate with white flowers...

00:34:38.980 --> 00:34:41.600
I guess he's not going to the
race circuit today, Lieutenant.

00:34:58.730 --> 00:34:59.860
Hey! Tap the call!

00:35:00.400 --> 00:35:00.690
Yes, sir!

00:35:05.570 --> 00:35:06.400
Hurry up!

00:35:06.940 --> 00:35:10.370
I can't. I'm unable to tap in because
he's using a special frequency!

00:35:11.540 --> 00:35:15.810
I don't want to hear any excuses.
You're the one responsible for all this!

00:35:16.610 --> 00:35:19.110
I understand. Yes, well, the thing is...

00:35:19.650 --> 00:35:23.850
If we judge the situation as dangerous,
we will take matters into our own hands.

00:35:24.160 --> 00:35:27.560
And when that happens your life
will no longer be guaranteed.

00:35:28.560 --> 00:35:31.430
Please understand! I've been
doing the best I can!

00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:32.890
I'll contact you again.

00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:38.090
Hello? Hello? Hello?

00:35:39.840 --> 00:35:40.960
Shit!

00:35:43.710 --> 00:35:45.140
Goddamn it...

00:35:58.290 --> 00:35:59.780
Where's Rie?

00:36:00.930 --> 00:36:02.760
Why won't Rie come to visit me?

00:36:04.700 --> 00:36:05.750
I don't know.

00:36:07.230 --> 00:36:09.960
She's probably shivering from the cold.

00:36:11.840 --> 00:36:13.130
In the summertime?

00:36:21.410 --> 00:36:25.310
Rie Fujinami had not come by
the hospital in five days.

00:36:26.850 --> 00:36:29.580
She may have been flaking out,
but it was still strange...

00:36:30.020 --> 00:36:33.720
She was worried about Yumiko
more than herself.

00:36:38.100 --> 00:36:40.000
Make a left at the next intersection.

00:36:42.970 --> 00:36:43.990
Right here is fine.

00:36:56.280 --> 00:36:57.410
Who's there?

00:37:00.250 --> 00:37:01.650
Who's there?

00:37:03.220 --> 00:37:04.350
Yumiko?

00:37:05.360 --> 00:37:06.360
Kaori?

00:37:06.360 --> 00:37:07.790
Oh, it's you Kaori...

00:37:13.330 --> 00:37:17.700
Look. Look, they wilted...
My cactuses...

00:37:19.070 --> 00:37:20.830
They used to be so pretty...

00:37:23.440 --> 00:37:25.240
They've completely dried up...

00:37:26.410 --> 00:37:29.850
They're gone... They left me all alone!

00:37:40.090 --> 00:37:42.820
Who are you? Go away!

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:54.230
It's cold... I'm so cold...

00:37:55.440 --> 00:37:58.770
She was obviously having
drug withdrawal symptoms.

00:38:02.850 --> 00:38:04.440
Come. Let's go...

00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:11.950
I couldn't allow Rie Fujinami to be
ruined at an age of sixteen...

00:38:13.090 --> 00:38:15.250
That was the only thing on my mind...

00:38:28.710 --> 00:38:33.470
Welcome. Your party is waiting for you
at a table, over by the window.

00:38:35.810 --> 00:38:37.370
What a surprise!

00:38:38.050 --> 00:38:41.140
I never thought the day would come
when you'd call to see me.

00:38:41.520 --> 00:38:42.990
I want you to look at this.

00:38:46.890 --> 00:38:48.530
You're kidding me.

00:38:48.530 --> 00:38:52.120
South American Pueruto.
Also known as Party of the Heavens.

00:38:52.800 --> 00:38:55.930
It's a recently discovered narcotic
plant that's out on the streets.

00:38:56.870 --> 00:38:59.030
From what I hear,
even a prick to the finger...

00:38:59.100 --> 00:39:01.870
will cause intense hallucinations
when the flower is in bloom.

00:39:02.740 --> 00:39:04.640
This must be what
you were investigating.

00:39:05.910 --> 00:39:09.570
You're an idiot. You think I'd leak
classified information to an outsider?

00:39:11.020 --> 00:39:15.010
This past spring four high school girls
went hiking on Mt. Sennin.

00:39:16.490 --> 00:39:18.920
It was my idea...

00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:22.220
I said the four of us should
do something special...

00:39:22.290 --> 00:39:25.390
before we finish sophomore year and
got separated the following year.

00:39:29.530 --> 00:39:32.900
But we lost our way in the thick fog...

00:39:33.770 --> 00:39:36.740
Then when we accidentally
stumbled across a flower garden...

00:39:38.010 --> 00:39:41.770
It was a field of cactuses
with red and pink flowers.

00:39:43.080 --> 00:39:45.550
Yuki was the first one
who pricked herself.

00:39:48.820 --> 00:39:51.880
It feels so good...
My body feels so tingly...

00:39:54.530 --> 00:39:56.580
She's right...

00:39:58.060 --> 00:40:00.530
Everyone was high...

00:40:06.140 --> 00:40:11.400
We each decided to take some
cactuses when we left the mountain.

00:40:17.110 --> 00:40:18.550
Seven days after their hike...

00:40:18.620 --> 00:40:21.180
Yuki Nakajima was killed
in a hit and run accident.

00:40:23.250 --> 00:40:23.780
Ten days later...

00:40:23.850 --> 00:40:26.060
Kaori Goto committed suicide by
stepping in front of a subway.

00:40:26.060 --> 00:40:28.490
There's a possibility it
may have been murder.

00:40:29.930 --> 00:40:30.950
And after two months,

00:40:31.030 --> 00:40:35.090
Yumiko Inoue and Rie Fujinami were
completely addicted to the Pueruto.

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:38.500
They left for Mr. Sennin to
get more of the cactuses...

00:40:38.570 --> 00:40:40.040
when the suspended bridge snapped.

00:40:45.210 --> 00:40:49.010
Which group is behind this?
The Mafia? Medejin Cartel?

00:40:49.650 --> 00:40:51.840
I can't comment until I have proof.

00:40:53.050 --> 00:40:55.850
Two sixteen year old girls
are already dead!

00:40:57.790 --> 00:41:01.120
My hands are tied...
I've got orders from above.

00:41:02.330 --> 00:41:05.450
On second thought, I don't think I ever
want to have a drink with you.

00:41:09.030 --> 00:41:09.860
Where are you going?

00:41:10.770 --> 00:41:14.330
Take care of Rie Fujinami
and Yumiko Inoue for me.

00:41:15.070 --> 00:41:16.300
You don't have to tell me.

00:41:16.370 --> 00:41:20.430
We've been watching them for some time,
before you even mentioned it.

00:41:37.160 --> 00:41:38.250
Look at you...

00:41:39.760 --> 00:41:44.330
Is that heroin, cocaine or
the newly available drug, Pueruto?

00:41:45.100 --> 00:41:46.090
At the rate you're going...

00:41:46.170 --> 00:41:48.730
you'll end up killing a patient
during a hernia operation.

00:41:53.980 --> 00:41:55.710
You're a disgrace.

00:41:56.010 --> 00:41:56.670
Leave me alone!

00:41:57.920 --> 00:42:01.450
I hear your family has owned
Mt. Sennin for generations.

00:42:01.450 --> 00:42:02.920
So what?

00:42:03.420 --> 00:42:07.930
You offered Mt. Sennin to the syndicate
so they can secretly cultivate Pueruto.

00:42:07.930 --> 00:42:08.960
I don't know anything!

00:42:08.960 --> 00:42:13.060
And you tried to kill the high school
girls that saw your secret nursery.

00:42:13.660 --> 00:42:16.330
I have nothing to do with that!
I don't know anything!

00:42:17.270 --> 00:42:19.240
I knew drugs were involved...

00:42:19.300 --> 00:42:23.240
when the urine and blood samples
tested positive for mescaline.

00:42:24.240 --> 00:42:26.900
To keep Yumiko Inoue in
a comatose state...

00:42:26.980 --> 00:42:29.170
you were administering drugs
on a regular basis.

00:42:29.550 --> 00:42:32.210
I don't know! I don't know anything!

00:42:33.280 --> 00:42:37.150
Tough luck for you, but I'm raising my
surgical fee from fifty million yen...

00:42:37.520 --> 00:42:40.350
to five hundred million yen!
I want it readied now.

00:42:41.630 --> 00:42:43.790
The syndicate will have
that kind of money.

00:42:44.190 --> 00:42:45.960
You'll be killed!

00:42:46.730 --> 00:42:50.600
Perhaps... but they might
go down before I do...

00:42:51.140 --> 00:42:51.730
You're crazy...

00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:54.960
Being crazy is how you play the game!

00:43:09.190 --> 00:43:12.380
You're supposed to call... You're
supposed to call before you come here!

00:43:12.690 --> 00:43:16.750
Tokio... We've decided to
pull out of this country...

00:43:19.360 --> 00:43:21.630
after we clean up our facilities...

00:44:15.290 --> 00:44:17.950
(Okay! Set them for 15 minutes!)

00:44:21.430 --> 00:44:22.760
(Let's go!)

00:44:28.300 --> 00:44:31.860
Hi Tokio. Hope you have
a pleasant dream.

00:44:49.050 --> 00:44:51.950
I felt like I was floating in mid air.

00:44:56.860 --> 00:44:59.950
I saw several beautiful
hallucinogenic imageries.

00:45:04.840 --> 00:45:07.030
My brain is melting...

00:45:12.140 --> 00:45:13.010
It's so quiet...

00:45:13.880 --> 00:45:15.370
Not a care in the world...

00:45:19.980 --> 00:45:23.890
Pulse 40... Maximum blood
pressure level around 60...

00:45:23.890 --> 00:45:25.580
I'm right before I go into shock...

00:45:26.060 --> 00:45:28.020
The effects are similar to opium...

00:45:29.260 --> 00:45:31.450
Yes... Yes... I'm going to be fine...

00:45:32.430 --> 00:45:36.590
As I dissolved into a state of ecstasy
I spoke to my other self...

00:45:38.570 --> 00:45:40.060
I'm going to be fine...

00:45:40.500 --> 00:45:43.800
There's a part of me who would
never give in to something like this...

00:45:45.110 --> 00:45:49.310
I have a black box that has overcome
despair and death, many times...

00:45:49.380 --> 00:45:50.510
he says.

00:45:55.990 --> 00:45:59.120
The black box is commanding me...

00:45:59.120 --> 00:46:01.090
You mustn't give up now!

00:47:06.520 --> 00:47:07.250
Um...

00:47:07.860 --> 00:47:10.730
Um, will we meet again?

00:47:11.500 --> 00:47:13.960
Coincidence doesn't happen a third time.

00:47:21.270 --> 00:47:22.740
I guess you're right.

00:47:25.010 --> 00:47:26.570
That is, until now...

00:48:11.590 --> 00:48:18.430
The city I returned to...

00:48:18.430 --> 00:48:24.840
wasn't how I remembered it.

00:48:24.840 --> 00:48:37.450
Glass walls were endlessly erected.

00:48:37.450 --> 00:48:44.220
"I want you to wait for me."

00:48:44.220 --> 00:48:51.130
The whispers I swallowed that day...

00:48:51.130 --> 00:48:57.940
"I want you to wait for me."

00:48:57.940 --> 00:49:06.540
My wound opens up now
as if it were fresh.

00:49:06.540 --> 00:49:10.250
Between the gaps of
the high-rise buildings...

00:49:10.250 --> 00:49:13.720
The moonlight comes through.

00:49:13.720 --> 00:49:19.990
Are you also looking for someone?

00:49:19.990 --> 00:49:23.660
It will never change...

00:49:23.660 --> 00:49:26.830
Peace is far beyond our journey.

00:49:26.830 --> 00:49:32.270
Does it only exist beyond the skies?

00:49:35.510 --> 00:49:40.070
But I'll be back again.

00:49:41.480 --> 00:49:45.480
Subtitle translation by
MAYUMI KOBAYASHI

00:49:45.480 --> 00:49:49.440
Subtitles by
JUSTIN SEVAKIS
